+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

Please note that the launchers require high openfiles limits, see
login.conf(5).

This package provides Winetricks and launchers for Steam and GOG Galaxy
using the 64-bit Wine port. Applications requiring 32-bit Windows support
may fail. Client binaries and Windows components are downloaded on demand
and remain subject to their respective licenses.

Run these commands as your normal desktop user:

    wine-steam
    wine-gog

Both launchers use WINEPREFIX, defaulting to $HOME/.wine. To keep separate
prefixes, use the same setting each time you launch the corresponding client:

    WINEPREFIX="$HOME/.wine-steam" wine-steam
    WINEPREFIX="$HOME/.wine-gog" wine-gog

Steam is extracted from Valve's update packages after SHA-256 verification.
GOG Galaxy is extracted from its installer after SHA-256 verification and
uses Winetricks to install its MFC and DirectX components. Both launchers
configure Liberation font replacements. Steam disables the CEF sandbox;
GOG Galaxy disables the Qt WebEngine sandbox and selects OpenGL.

To install components into a client's prefix, close its Windows applications
and use the same WINEPREFIX with Winetricks, for example:

    WINEPREFIX="$HOME/.wine-steam" winetricks arial

See winetricks(1) for available recipes. The optional Winetricks GUI requires
Zenity or KDialog, installed separately.
